Large language models are remarkably good at sounding confident about numbers they've invented. That's a real risk when the number is your tax bill.

## The temptation, and why we didn't take it

It would be easy to let an AI "just compute" your tax from a description of your income — it would feel magical, right up until it hallucinated a rate band or missed a credit, silently and convincingly.

## What the AI actually does

Salli's AI reads your documents, drafts entries for your approval, and explains results in plain language. Every number it shows you was produced by a deterministic engine running a versioned, chartered-accountant-reviewed rule pack — never generated by the model itself.

## Why this is safer, not slower

A deterministic engine gives the same answer to the same inputs, every time, and records exactly which rule produced each figure. That's what makes a number reproducible years later, and what makes it something you can actually stand behind — not just something that sounded plausible.
